Requirements
Requirement	Module	Access program	Statement
system-generation.1	system generation	values	The access program values MUST give the Values as values reads them, handing it the folder of values' own file, as module folder gives it.
values.1	values	values	The access program values MUST read the Values from values.mtsv in the folder it is handed, the Values sheet of this specification as each package carries it, by the header Value and Given, giving relation Values of the domains Value and Given.
values.2	values		values.mtsv MUST be written from the Values sheet of this specification, its Value and Given columns, as the generator writes a sheet.
values.3	values	values	A values.mtsv that cannot be read, or that the parser rejects, MUST end values as not MTSV.
distribution-package.1	distribution package		python/pyproject.toml MUST declare the build system the Values build requires and build backend name, and the project: name void-os, the version, requires-python, the dependency the Value python dependency mcp gives, license MIT, the [project.scripts] entry of the void-os command, and values.mtsv as package data, and no other table or field.
distribution-package.2	distribution package		javascript/package.json MUST declare the name void-os, the version, the type module, the bin entry of the void-os command naming src/void-os.js, the engines the Value node engine gives, the dependencies the Values javascript dependency server and javascript dependency zod give, the license MIT, its files the folder src alone, which holds values.mtsv, and the mcpName the Value registry name gives, and no other field.
distribution-package.3	distribution package		server.json MUST name the server by the Value registry name, describe it by the Value server description, and list two packages, the npm package and the PyPI package, each named void-os, at the version, each run with no argument over stdio.
distribution-package.4	distribution package		Each README MUST say what void-os is, as scope.1 says it, and how it is installed: pipx install void-os for the PyPI package and npm install --global void-os for the npm package; lay out the modules as the Modules sheet's tree, each by its secret on one line; and, for the PyPI package, hold the Value registry name as the registry's ownership verification names it.
distribution-package.5	distribution package		Each LICENSE MUST be the MIT License's text, its copyright line the Value copyright holders.
runner.1	runner	run	The access program run MUST find the case by its requirement and case among the cases of the file, in the folder conformance it is handed, of the requirement's module, and never by its place on disk, and read the books from the folder spec of the repository, the folder that holds the runner's own file at the path the Files sheet gives it, as module folder gives that file's folder.
runner.2	runner	run	A case MUST be run in an empty directory made for it, its resolved pathname $PWD, $PWD/home the user's home folder by the variable the platform reads it from, TZ set to UTC0 and each variable of environment, and no other variable set but PATH and those the platform needs to start a program.
runner.3	runner	run	Each fixture placed before, of the file of the case's module or of a node above, MUST be placed at its pathname before the call, the directories its pathname needs made.
runner.4	runner	run	The case's access program, where it starts no component, MUST be called on the case's module, loaded from its files as the Files sheet places them in the repository, with the Values as values gives them, or the fixture the case places at its values argument, the case's arguments and the fixtures placed at an argument, by the positions of the Parameters sheet, then each module Compositions hands that module, loaded the same way.
runner.5	runner	run	Each result of type JSON text MUST be compared by its instances, every instance result instances names and no other, each line of standard output by the instances stdout lines names, and each file of file instances by the instances it names, run giving each comparison that does not hold.
runner.6	runner	run	$PWD, $HOME, $INPUT and $REPOSITORY MUST be expanded in every value, and nothing else: $HOME/Documents the user's documents folder as PLATFORMDIRS gives it for the platform the case runs on, each / of a pathname the platform's separator, $INPUT $PWD as name within a folder writes it, and $REPOSITORY the repository runner.1 reads the books from.
runner.7	runner	run	A value MUST be read as the Written column of its type writes it.
runner.20	runner	run	A field compared, whose column the Domains rows of the relation its sheet is named by give the type time, MUST match any date-time RFC 3339 writes with the offset Z.
runner.21	runner	run	A text read as a JSON text that JSON text rejects MUST be read as holding no instance.
runner.8	runner	run	A case whose module and access program are empty MUST call nothing, each pathname it names being a file of the repository, relative to it.
runner.9	runner	run	A requirement and case that name no case MUST end run as no case.
runner.10	runner	run	A file of conformance the parser rejects MUST end run as not MTSV.
runner.11	runner	run	The case's access program, where it starts a component, MUST be run as the component's command starts it: a child process in $PWD with the environment of runner.2 alone, its program the command line of the Given of the Value the component's Command names, from the repository runner.1 reads the books from, its operands then the case's arguments; its standard input the case's stdin, each line then LF, in UTF-8, written when it starts, and closed once the lines of standard output read hold a response for each request among the lines written, or standard output ends, a request being a line that holds a JSON object with the members method and id, and a response a line that holds a JSON object with the member id and the member result or error; its standard output the lines read, then the rest.
runner.22	runner	run	A started component's exit status MUST be the result 1, its standard output what output, stdout lines and the fixture placed at - compare, and its standard error what diagnostic and reason compare.
runner.12	runner	run	Each file of octets MUST be placed at its pathname before the call, its octets those of the file it names, beside the file of the case's module or of a node above, nothing in it expanded, the directories its pathname needs made, and its modification time, where modified gives one, set that many seconds before the call.
runner.13	runner	run	Each zip package of zip entries MUST be placed at its pathname before the call, the directories its pathname needs made, written as ZIP-APPNOTE writes a ZIP file, its entries in order, each with its name, its method and the CRC-32 of its text in UTF-8, its data that text compressed by DEFLATE where its method is 8 and held as it is otherwise.
runner.14	runner	run	Each database of database statements MUST be placed at its pathname before the call, the directories its pathname needs made, built by running its statements in order on a new database there.
runner.15	runner	run	The error the call ends with, with its reason where the case gives one, whether standard output holds anything and whether standard error holds a diagnostic, where the case gives them, and each result of results, as its text, MUST be compared, run giving each comparison that does not hold.
runner.16	runner	run	Each fixture placed after MUST be compared as its sheets with what is at its pathname: a file, standard output, or a result, run giving each comparison that does not hold.
runner.17	runner	run	Each pathname of absent MUST hold nothing after the call, run giving each that does.
runner.18	runner	run	Each expected file MUST hold, after the call, the octets of the file it names, beside the file of the case's module or of a node above, run giving each that does not.
runner.19	runner	run	Each text of file texts MUST be held within one of the lines, or the incomplete line, of the file it names, run giving each that is not.
